@talks work:infirmary
// TW1, the Talk a while work pools: Infirmary (plans/work-pools-plan.html, decided 2026-10-20). Ids
// work.infirmary.<slug>; topic always "work". Never anyone's medical details. Oduya (Counsellor) skips the wound and
// bone talks; the "listening" talks suit him, kept clear of grief (his thread is loss). Rina: never the exam or why
// she wants to be a doctor (her arc). Nandakumar has her own talks. Grieve (exams), Larsen (notgood): no doubt talk.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- acquaintance: the job up close

== beds
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:nandakumar|oduya
them: Changed every bed in here before breakfast. Corners tight. Nobody's slept in one all week.
them: That's a good week, in the infirmary. Empty beds and a tidy cupboard.   #warm
ask: What does a good week look like in your job?
listen: Do you ever wish it was busier?
  them: Never. Bored is good, in here. Bored means everyone's well.
share: A quiet board. Nothing breaking.
  them: Same as us, then. A quiet week's a kind week.   #warm
cheer: Seconds at dinner, every night.
  them: That's not a week. That's a dream. Drink some water with it.   #funny

== night-doctor
when: tier>=acquaintance who:yoon-elif
them: Three in the morning, someone comes in with a cough that's really can't-sleep.
them: Tea, a blanket, ten minutes of talk. Most nights that's the whole treatment.   #warm
ask: What helps you, when you can't sleep?
listen: Do you mind the night shift?
  them: I like it. People talk more at three. They've taken the day's armour off.   #warm
share: Talking to someone. Or a book.
  them: Both good medicine. The book's quieter.   #funny
cheer: Counting the rungs on my bunk ladder.
  them: How many? No, don't tell me. I'll count mine tonight.   #funny

== blood-types
when: tier>=acquaintance who:grieve-thea|larsen-hamid|nordqvist-dmitri|rina
them: I know everyone's blood type. Not on purpose. It just went in, like song words.
them: Pass someone in the corridor and their type pops up. It's a very odd superpower.   #funny
ask: What's something you know without meaning to?
listen: Do you know mine?
  them: Of course. Not telling. Medical records are private. Even the fun ones.
share: Which panels stick, all over the ship.
  them: That's a superpower too. More useful at parties.   #funny
cheer: Everyone's favourite biscuit.
  them: Brennan has that one in a book. You're competing with a professional.   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- colleague: why this job and listening

== bench
when: tier>=colleague !who:nandakumar
them: People think the hard part's the cuts and burns. It's not. It's the bench by the door.
them: Someone sits on the bench pretending they're fine. You learn to see it from the door.
ask: How do you tell, when someone's not all right?
listen: How do you see it?
  them: They sit very straight. Fine people slouch. Nobody believes me. It's true.   #funny
share: They go quiet. Or too loud.
  them: That's it exactly. You'd be good in here.   #warm
cheer: They say "I'm fine" twice.
  them: Twice is the giveaway. Once is usually true.   #warm

== just-listen
when: tier>=colleague !who:nandakumar
them: Half of what we do is listen. Properly. Not waiting to talk. Just listening.
them: People leave lighter. Nothing's been fixed. Something's been heard.   #warm
ask: Who's the best listener you know?
listen: How do you listen properly?
  them: Stop planning what to say back. That's all. It's harder than it sounds.
share: Someone at home. They never interrupted.
  them: Rare and precious. I hope you tell them, sometime.   #warm
cheer: The lift. It never interrupts.
  them: True. Terrible advice, though. Very short conversations.   #funny

== bandage-hands
when: tier>=colleague !who:nandakumar|oduya|rina !thread:exams
them: I chose this job for my hands. They're steady. Always have been. Even when I'm not.
them: Somebody once said steady hands are a gift you should give away. So I do.   #warm
ask: What's a gift you have that you give away?
listen: Are you ever nervous, then?
  them: Inside, yes. My hands don't know. I've never told them.   #funny
share: Patience. I'm good at waiting.
  them: Then you give it away daily. People are grateful. Even when they don't say.   #warm
cheer: Opening stuck jars.
  them: Underrated. The galley would hire you on the spot.   #funny

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- friend: what it means

== infirmary-means
when: tier>=friend !who:nandakumar|rina
them: What does the infirmary mean to me? Nobody aboard is ever alone when they're poorly.
them: Three in the morning, middle of a storm, there's always someone here. Tonight, maybe me.   #warm
ask: Who do you do the job for, if you had to say?
listen: Does it ever feel like too much?
  them: Some days. Then someone says thanks with their eyes and it's light again.   #warm
share: The people who'll never know I did it.
  them: Then we're the same. Quiet care. The best kind.   #warm
cheer: For the biscuits in the drawer.
  them: Medical supplies. Strictly. Sometimes.   #funny

== listening-habit
when: tier>=friend !who:nandakumar
them: The job gave me a habit. I listen to how people breathe. The mess, the lift, everywhere.
them: Fast, slow, a sigh. You can tell a whole day from it. I try not to. I can't stop.   #warm
ask: Has your work left you with a habit you can't switch off?
listen: What does my breathing say?
  them: That you've had a full day and you're glad to sit down. Good diagnosis, that.   #warm
share: I check every lamp I walk past.
  them: Same family of habit. We're both always on duty, a little.
cheer: I count biscuits in tins.
  them: That's not a habit. That's a calling.   #funny
